      "content": "While I understand the desire for practical shortcuts, training manuals must emphasize objective, observable actions over generalizations about demographics. Instead of profiling groups, train staff to recognize group dynamics that disrupt luxury ambiance: large numbers congregating outside assigned areas, loud volume levels, or persistent loitering late at night. By focusing on behaviors that clash with your hotel's standards, you maintain fairness while ensuring proactive service.",
